XU_FINAL374_FM_API_BEGIN	man	set_host_options
2.  Synopsys Commands                                        Command Reference
                               set_host_options

NAME
       set_host_options
              Sets options for parallel processing.

SYNTAX
       status set_host_options
              [ -max_cores num_cores ]
              [ -local_process ]

   Data Types
              num_cores string

ARGUMENTS
       -max_cores num_cores
              Specifies the number of processes on the local machine to use in
              parallel.  The default is one core.  The maximum number of cores
              you  can  specify  is eight.  A second Formality license is con-
              sumed if you specify more than four cores.  The second  licensed
              is not released until Formality exits.

       -local_process
              Specifies  that -max_cores applies to the local process. This is
              always true for now and may always be omitted.

DESCRIPTION
       This command sets options for parallel processing.

EXAMPLES
       This example specifies that up to 4 processes may be used on the  local
       machine in parallel.
         fm_shell> set_host_options -max_cores 4

SEE ALSO
                          Version R-2020.09-SP5
            Copyright (c) 2021 Synopsys, Inc. All rights reserved.
XU_FINAL374_FM_API_END	man	set_host_options	1	0
