XU_FINAL374_FM_API_BEGIN	man	report_not_compared_points
2.  Synopsys Commands                                        Command Reference
                          report_not_compared_points

NAME
       report_not_compared_points
              Reports compare points that it was unnecessary to compare.

SYNTAX
       int report_not_compared_points
              [-compare_rule]
              [-substring substring]
              [-point_type point_type]
              [-status status]
              [-except_status except_status]
              [-list]

   Data Types
              substring string
              point_type string
              status string
              except_status string

   Enabled Shell Modes
       Match
       Verify

ARGUMENTS
       -compare_rule
              Reports  mapped  object  names resulting from the application of
              compare rules.

       -substring substring
              Reports only the points containing the specified substring.

       -point_type point_type
              Filters the report to include only the compare points with char-
              acteristics  that match the specified type or types. By default,
              all compare point  types  are  included.  Specify  one  or  more
              point_type values on which to report.

              The valid point_type values are as follows:
                o bbox_pin - Report all black-box pin compare points.
                o bbox_input - Report black-box input pin compare points.
                o  bbox_inout  -  Report  black-box  bidirectional pin compare
                points.
                o loop - Report loop compare points.
                o bbox_net - Report black-box-resolved multiply-driven nets.
                o cut - Report cut-points.
                o port - Report all port compare points.
                o output - Report output port compare points.
                o inout - Report bidirectional port compare points.
                o directly_undriven_output - Report output  and  bidirectional
                ports  that  do  not have a connected net, or that have a con-
                nected net but do not have a driving pin.
                o reg - Report all register compare points.
                o DFF - Report flip-flop register compare points.
                o LAT - Report latch register compare points.
                o trans - Report transparent latch register compare points.
                o PDCut - Report power domain pin compare points.
                o PGPin  -  Report  power/ground/power-down  function  compare
                points.

       -status status
              Reports  only the points that match the specified type or types.
              If both -status and -point_type are specified,  included  points
              must pass both filters.

              The valid status values are as follows:
                o none - Report all except these special types.
                o trans - Report transparent latch registers.
                o const - Report all constant registers.
                o const0 - Report constant 0 registers.
                o const1 - Report constant 1 registers.
                o constX - Report constant X registers.
                o const0X - Report constrained 0X registers.
                o const1X - Report constrained 1X registers.
                o clock_gate - Report clock-gate latches.
                o dont_verify - Report dont_verify points.
                o unread - Report unread points.
                o undriven - Report undriven points.
                o inverted - Report points matched inverted.
                o noninverted - Report points matched noninverted.
                o targeted - Report points targeted for verification.
                o not_targeted - Report points not targeted for verification.

       -except_status except_status
              Filters  the  report  to exclude points that match the specified
              type.  Multiple occurrences of this switch are legal and  values
              are additive.  The valid except_status values are as follows:

                o trans - Exclude transparent latch registers.
                o const - Exclude all constant registers.
                o const0 - Exclude constant 0 registers.
                o const1 - Exclude constant 1 registers.
                o constX - Exclude constant X registers.
                o const0X - Exclude constrained 0X registers.
                o const1X - Exclude constrained 1X registers.
                o clock_gate - Exclude clock-gate latches.
                o dont_verify - Exclude dont_verify points.
                o unread - Exclude unread points.
                o undriven - Exclude undriven points.
                o inverted - Exclude points matched inverted.
                o noninverted - Exclude points matched noninverted.
                o targeted - Exclude points targeted for verification.
                o not_targeted - Exclude points not targeted for verification.

       -list  Reports the not compared points as a list. You can use this list
              for further Tcl processing.

DESCRIPTION
       The report_not_compared_points command reports points that it  was  not
       necessary  to compare because they were either unread, constant, marked
       dont_verify, or clock-gating latches.

       Formality produces a report that includes the total  number  of  points
       reported  followed  by  each  pair  of matched design objects. For each
       design object, the report lists the matching method, whether the  match
       occurred  in  the  most  recent  matching operation, the container, the
       design object type, and the design object's designID.

EXAMPLES
       The following example  reports  on  all  of  the  not  compared  design
       objects:

         prompt> report_not_compared_points

         27 Not compared points:

           Ref  LATCG      Name(Last) ref:/LAPLACE_LIB/laplace/emif0/emif_clocks0/clkgate_inp_sb
           Impl LATCG      Name(Last) der:/LAPLACE_LIB/laplace/emif0/emif_clocks0/clkgate_inp_sb

           Ref  LATCG      Name(Last) ref:/LAPLACE_LIB/laplace/emif0/emif_clocks0/clkgate_inp_sd
           Impl LATCG      Name(Last) der:/LAPLACE_LIB/laplace/emif0/emif_clocks0/clkgate_inp_sd

           Ref  LAT        Name(Last) ref:/LAPLACE_LIB/laplace/emif0/emif_clocks0/clkgate_inp_tck
